add('Environment','04 · Ocean carbon removal','Marine CDR: permanence, additionality and ecosystem risk','The issue reviews interest in ocean-based removal methods.','Approaches discussed include coastal ecosystem restoration and more experimental ocean-chemistry/biomass interventions.|Gross uptake is not necessarily durable net atmospheric removal once leakage, reversals and energy use are considered.|Measurement, reporting and verification remain central scientific/governance challenges.','Avoided emissions and removed atmospheric carbon are different accounting claims; neither permits double counting.','AP coastal projects must protect fisheries, biodiversity and community consent alongside carbon measurement.|Do not treat restoring mangroves and large-scale ocean alkalinity modification as having identical evidence or risk.','Marine removal complements rather than replaces deep emissions cuts; a pilot is not proof of safe gigatonne-scale deployment.','What safeguards should precede large-scale marine carbon-removal claims?',src='',slug='marine-carbon-dioxide-removal-mcdr')
add('Environment','05 · Big-cat cooperation','IBCA: seven species, range countries and actual membership','The issue reports Saudi Arabia joining the conservation alliance.','The seven focal cats are tiger, lion, leopard, snow leopard, cheetah, jaguar and puma.|Range-country eligibility is broader than the count of countries that have formally joined.|Habitat connectivity, prey and conflict mitigation matter alongside species-specific protection.','An international coalition’s announcement, treaty status, membership and field implementation should be dated separately.','For AP, connect habitat conservation with locally occurring species and institutions; do not infer all seven cats naturally occur in India.|Avoid copying the article’s inconsistent five-year/fiscal-year funding description as a verified appropriation period.','IBCA is not evidence that all95potential range countries are members, or that jaguar/puma have wild Indian ranges.','How can international species cooperation support habitat-level conservation?',src='',slug='international-big-cat-alliance-ibca-4')
add('Environment','06 · Dam systems and safety','Dam safety: structural integrity and downstream preparedness','The issue reviews rehabilitation and safety modernisation.','Dam management addresses inspection, operation, maintenance, emergency planning and responsibility, not only construction.|Sedimentation can reduce usable storage even where a dam wall remains structurally sound.|DRIPfinancing/rehabilitation and statutory safety bodies are complementary, not identical interventions.','Reservoir storage, design flood, gate operation and downstream exposure together determine risk; age alone does not identify failure probability.','For AP, use basin-level forecasting, rule curves, independent review and warning protocols alongside repairs.|Differentiate the inventory definitions of large/specified dams rather than repeat undated totals as exact current coverage.','Do not call a safety audit proof of zero future risk or assume a newly built project requires no operational preparedness.','Design a lifecycle approach to dam safety in a changing climate.',src='',slug='dam-safety-in-india-1')
add('Geography','01 · ENSO and forecast uncertainty','“Super” El Niño: probability is not destiny','The issue discusses a potential strong event later in2026.','ENSO couples tropical Pacific ocean-temperature and atmospheric-circulation anomalies.|“Super El Niño” is an informal intensity description, not a separate fourth ENSO phase.|Monsoon impacts are probabilistic and interact with the Indian Ocean, intraseasonal variability and regional conditions.','A forecast of a driver does not establish the realised rainfall at every Indian district or deterministic drought.','For AP, update sowing advice, irrigation budgeting and heat plans using issued forecasts and local conditions.|Do not treat an earlier magazine forecast as the latest November outlook or a century-record event already observed.','El Niño does not mean drought in every part of India every year; a probability must retain its issue date and lead time.','How should climate-risk planning use seasonal probabilities without overstating certainty?',src='',slug='super-el-nino-1')
add('Science & Technology','01 · AI-enabled weather services','Weather AI: resolution, lead time and skill are different','The issue describes new monsoon and high-resolution forecast products.','The monsoon-advance product provides probabilistic guidance up to four weeks ahead.|The1-kmrainfall product discussed is a pilot for Uttar Pradesh, not proof of identical AP deployment.|IMD,IITMPune and NCMRWFare identified as collaborating institutions.','Higher spatial resolution is a grid characteristic, not an automatic guarantee of greater accuracy or decision usefulness.','AP users need calibrated forecast skill, local advisories and dissemination in accessible formats.|Combine AI products with observations, uncertainty communication and impact-based decisions rather than replace accountable forecasters.','Do not confuse monsoon advance with total seasonal rainfall or extend a UPpilot’s coverage to all India.','What makes AI weather guidance operationally useful rather than only technically impressive?',src='',slug='ai-enabled-weather-forecasting-systems')
