add('Science & Technology','02 · Research governance','Ease of R&D: predictable support and accountable autonomy','The issue discusses NITI Aayog’s research-administration report.','The report diagnoses delayed fellowships, compliance burdens and weak research–industry links.|Recommendations include professional research offices, better grant administration and technology-transfer capacity.|A proposed target of2%GDPfor research is an aspiration, not a statement that spending already reached it.','GERD, government budget provision, actual expenditure and research output have different denominators and timing.','AP universities need timely support, ethical review and freedom to pursue quality research, not only more MoUs or patent counts.|Evaluate commercialisation alongside open science, reproducibility and public-interest research that may not yield an immediate licence.','Do not call a recommended digital fellowship platform an already universal service or assume all patents become useful products.','How can India reduce research friction without weakening scientific accountability?',src='',slug='ease-of-doing-research-development-rd-in-india')
