add('Culture & History','01 · Bhojshala — heritage and legal status','Bhojshala: distinguish archaeology, attribution and current orders','The issue discusses litigation over the Dhar monument.','Bhojshala–Kamal Maula complex is in Dhar,Madhya Pradesh, with layered inscriptions, architecture and worship claims.|The magazine reports a High Court decision; the underlying full judgment and any later stay/appeal have not been independently reviewed here.|Heritage conservation and religious-rights questions engage distinct statutory and constitutional tests.','An archaeological interpretation, historical patronage attribution and operative court direction are different kinds of claims.','For Mains, focus on evidence-led conservation, lawful access arrangements and protection from damage or inflammatory inference.|Do not copy the article’s erroneous gloss of Kurma as crocodile: Kurma means tortoise; specific inscription authorship needs separate verification.','Do not certify present ownership/worship rights or final litigation status from a monthly summary, or extend one site’s dispute to other communities/monuments.','How should heritage disputes be managed through evidence, law and conservation?',src='',slug='bhojshala-temple')
