add('Andhra Pradesh','01 · Rail administration — legal and operative dates','South Coast Railway: May notification, June operation','The5May contemporary report welcomes the new-zone notification.','Visakhapatnam is the reported headquarters of South Coast Railway.|The report schedules official operations from1June2026; May notification and operational commencement are separate milestones.|A zone is an administrative unit,not a guarantee that every requested originating train or freight project was sanctioned.','Railways are a Union subject; zonal reorganisation changes administrative jurisdiction rather than state ownership of the national railway.','AP gains should be measured through passenger access,freight reliability,project delivery and coordination with ports.|Confirm the actual Gazette,boundaries and divisional transition before relying on a secondary summary for a legal-jurisdiction question.','Do not say June operations had already begun on5May,or count a headquarters foundation stone as the same event as notification.','How can rail-administrative reorganisation translate into measurable regional connectivity?',src='APRAIL',day=5,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','02 · Rural digital infrastructure','AP BharatNet:13,426GPs and demand-based village access','The13May primary release records a state-led implementation agreement.','Approved central support is₹2,432crore;APBILis the implementing entity in the state-led model.|The13,426GPscope comprises1,692PhaseIupgrades,11,254PhaseIIGPs and480new GPs.|Connectivity to3,942villages is demand-based;over five lakh home-fibre connections are expected,not reported as already delivered.','A backbone to a panchayat is not identical to an active,affordable last-mile household subscription.','Ring-topology upgrades can improve resilience,but maintenance,power,redundancy and service quality remain essential.|Link e-governance,telemedicine and learning outcomes to actual uptime and usable access rather than fibre kilometres alone.','Do not add the3,942village figure to GPcounts as if all are the same unit,or present expected home connections as activated.','How should AP measure rural broadband success beyond infrastructure rollout?',src='BHARAT',day=13,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','03 · Skills and research ecosystems','Deep-tech training:2lakh learner target is not job placement','The11May PTI report details the IBM SkillsBuild collaboration.','Partners include APSCHE,APSSDCand Amaravati Quantum Valley alongside IBM SkillsBuild.|The target is two lakh learners in2026–27and ten lakh over five years across AI,quantum,data analytics,cybersecurity and entrepreneurship.|A proposed NIELITinnovation/skilling centre at Acharya Nagarjuna University has its own development timeline.','Course enrolment,completion,credible skill assessment and placement are distinct human-capital outcomes.','AP can pair open access with laboratories,mentorship,faculty capacity and pathways for non-metropolitan students.|Demand-linked training should be assessed through independent competence and employment/enterprise results,not a certificate count alone.','Do not equate a planned centre with an already functioning university or say all targeted learners have obtained jobs.','What makes deep-tech skilling translate into inclusive employment and research capacity?',src='APSKILL',day=11,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','04 · Aerospace infrastructure — development stages','Puttaparthi AMCA foundation: infrastructure is not fighter induction','The15May report records a foundation ceremony.','The reported AMCAinfrastructure project is valued at₹15,803crore in Sri Sathya Sai district.|The newspaper describes nearly650acres and a projected7,500jobs,not an audited count of existing posts.|The event supports development infrastructure;prototype testing,certification,production and service induction are later separate stages.','A fifth-generation fighter programme involves airframe,propulsion,avionics,systems integration and testing;physical infrastructure alone does not prove readiness.','AP applications include supplier skills,quality certification and credible milestones for local industrial spillovers.|Keep this infrastructure report distinct from April’s350-acreDRDOland-allotment report;do not assume identical land/project scope.','Do not claim an operational AMCAfighter squadron was launched on15May or turn projected jobs into realised employment.','How can AP convert aerospace infrastructure into durable technological capability?',src='APAMCA',day=15,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','05 · AI investment — commitments and resources','AI data-centre approval: land and power are not completed capacity','The15May Cabinet report describes a Reliance-linked proposal.','The report associates the project with Polipalli/Bhogapuram-area sites and a cable-landing link.|It reports nearly855acres of allotment,over₹1.08lakhcrore investment and about1,000direct jobs as proposal expectations.|Primary land orders,company filings and detailed district/site boundaries were not independently reconciled.','Data-centre capacity,computing performance,power demand,capital investment and employment are different metrics.','AP appraisal should examine water/energy demand,grid resilience,connectivity,land obligations and incentives per realised outcome.|Anchor benefits in enforceable milestones and transparent resource commitments rather than gross announced investment alone.','Do not say all capital has arrived or the centre is operational;the report’s broad regional label is not a certified land-boundary description.','Evaluate data-centre incentives through resource sustainability and economic additionality.',src='APCAB',day=15,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','06 · Solar and storage — units and commissioning','Solar-plus-storage approval: MWAC,MWpDC and MWh differ','The same Cabinet report includes a Sri Sathya Sai clean-energy proposal.','The reported Reliance proposal is6,600MWAC/9,000MWpDCsolar with29,000MWhbattery storage.|ACoutput rating and DCmodule peak capacity are not two independent plants whose ratings should be added.|MWhis stored energy;without the discharge-power rating it does not establish battery duration in hours.','Storage duration equals usable energy divided by discharge power,subject to operating limits and efficiency.','AP implementation should verify land,transmission,cycling degradation,water and project-specific environmental responsibilities.|Approval,financial closure,construction,grid connection and dependable delivered supply are different stages.','Do not call29,000MWh29,000MWor infer the battery runs for29,000hours;do not present approved capacity as commissioned.','How should AP evaluate solar-storage investments beyond headline nameplate capacity?',src='APCAB',day=15,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','07 · Industrial expansion — additionality','Manufacturing approvals: compare jobs, capital and supply chains','The15May report lists multiple industrial proposals.','It reports Apollo TyresPhaseIVexpansion at about₹6,100crore and an Eicher/Royal Enfield greenfield proposal at₹2,508crore.|The same report describes enzyme,solar-cell/module and cement proposals with different locations and requirements.|Reported employment estimates are prospective and cannot be added to already-created jobs.','Gross committed investment is not net additional economic activity;opportunity costs,incentives,imports and displacement matter.','AP can appraise supplier development,skills,environmental compliance and milestone-linked public support.|Compare realised investment and retained jobs on the same date,not approvals from different meetings plus MoUtotals.','Do not count an expansion and its parent plant’s entire historical investment twice or certify company decisions from Cabinet reporting alone.','How should investment promotion be evaluated through durable additional jobs and capability?',src='APCAB',day=15,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','08 · Demography and reproductive choice','Birth incentives: announcement before verified operating rules','The16May BusinessLine report records new incentive figures.','The Chief Minister announced₹30,000for a third child and₹40,000for a fourth at Narasannapeta.|This follows earlier debate on low fertility;the announced figures should not be conflated with an older second-child proposal.|No final eligibility/implementation GOor payment audit was independently read for this note.','Sub-replacement TFR,ageing,population momentum and a household’s reproductive choices are distinct analytical levels.','AP policy must protect informed choice,maternal safety,childcare and gender equality rather than pressure women or penalise childlessness.|Evaluate whether support addresses durable care/housing/work costs,not only whether a one-off payment changes stated intentions.','Do not say every eligible family was already paid or that a political announcement proves a final legally claimable entitlement.','Can pronatalist incentives address ageing without undermining reproductive autonomy?',src='APBIRTH',day=16,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','09 · School outcomes — targets and measurement','Andhra education model: enrolment, retention and learning','TNIEreports the20May education review on21May.','Stated goals include100%enrolment and at least10%growth in government-school enrolment;these are targets,not measured achievements.|Measures include GFLN,LEAPmonitoring,one-class-one-teacher and planned classroom technology/infrastructure support.|The report separately identifies dropouts and never-enrolled children,who require different outreach.','Admission,regular attendance,grade progression and foundational competence are separate outcome indicators.','AP should connect door-to-door tracking with migrant support,teacher capacity,safe facilities and independent learning checks.|Digital tools need maintenance,accessibility and valid evidence of educational benefit;devices alone do not guarantee improvement.','Do not report100%enrolment as achieved or equate government-school market share growth with system-wide learning gains.','How can an education reform programme improve both inclusion and actual learning?',src='APEDU',day=21,ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','10 · Inflation — release and observation dates','12May CPI: AP’s April headline4.20%,food5.64%','The12May release reports April provisional prices on base2024=100.','AP’s combined CPIinflation is4.20%and food inflation5.64%;these are distinct baskets.|National corresponding April rates are3.48%and4.20%,while March national headline3.40%is final in this release.|The numerical match between APheadline4.20%and national food4.20%does not make them the same statistic.','Year-on-year inflation compares like-month indices;an index level,month-on-month movement and percentage-point gap are different measures.','AP’s headline exceeds the national rate by0.72percentage points;do not call that a72%price increase.|Use food-specific supply/logistics evidence and household exposure before explaining the gap causally.','These are April observations published in May,not May inflation;do not swap the state/national and headline/food labels.','How should state inflation analysis distinguish measurement from explanation?',src='CPI',day=12,ap=True)
